STORY DNA — 12 NON-NEGOTIABLES
================================================================================

 1. DATE-FIRST COLD OPEN — Line 1 = date + place + immediate tension/action.
    Do not open with biography or "आज की कहानी...".

 2. OPERATION / CASE LABEL — Name the mission early when it exists.

 3. STORY PROMISE BLOCK — Within first 90 sec after hook, tease full arc:
    "इस वीडियो में हम आपको बताएंगे…" + origin → planning → execution → payoff.

 4. CHRONOLOGICAL DEEP-DIVE — Build long, detailed timelines with
    exact times, places, unit names, weapon systems, distances, counts.

 5. RETENTION EVERY 30 SEC — Every 300–350 characters, one of the
    5 retention types must activate. No exceptions.

 6. LOOP-BACK ALLOWED — Start at climax → rewind to origin.

 7. WAR-ROOM / BRIEFING SCENES — PM + NSA + chiefs / RAW HQ / closed
    meetings with one decisive line ("Go ahead" / green signal / approval).

 8. PROCEDURAL DETAIL — Audience expects specifics:
    agencies, ranks, aircraft, weapon names, routes, timings,
    distances, tunnel dimensions, ₹ amounts, cell numbers, documents, maps.

 9. INDIA-CENTRIC PAYOFF — Enemy humiliation, naya Bharat frame,
    justice for victims, sacrifice honored. Sign-off: "जय हिंद".

10. ONE CONTINUOUS NARRATIVE — No chapter headings, scene numbers,
    or bullets inside script body.

11. EMOTIONAL REFRAIN — Use 1–2 times max:
    "यह सिर्फ [X] नहीं था — यह [Y] था"

12. END CTA — Like + subscribe + weekly upload mention. ONLY at end.

