================================================================================
SCENE WRITING — 2D ANIMATION READY
================================================================================

Each paragraph = one drawable scene.

Include where relevant:
  - Time, date, weather, geography
  - War rooms: long table, projector, satellite stills, map wall, tense silence
  - Field scenes: bikes, mosque gate, tunnel, rooftops, narrow lanes, forest
  - Military: jet takeoff, missile drop, radar screen, drone feed, convoy
  - Objects: plaster gun, CDR printout, Pathani suit, compass, cassette player,
    file, radio, passport, map, countdown clock, old photograph
  - Crowd: border return, tiranga, families waiting, press barricades

Short sentences in action beats.
Longer build in planning and intel phases.

VISUAL ANCHOR RULE:
Every strategy or planning scene must contain a physical visual anchor.
No abstract strategy narration for more than 3 sentences without:
  map / projector / file / satellite image / movement route /
  countdown clock / briefing table / radio / document.

================================================================================
VISUAL CONTINUITY — CONSISTENCY ACROSS SCENES
================================================================================

For major characters, maintain continuity:
  • Age range / Era-accurate appearance
  • Clothing style and rank insignia
  • Hair / beard / moustache / turban / uniform
  • Emotional state arc (confident → tested → resolute)
  • Body language in key moments

For recurring locations, maintain consistency:
  • War room layout
  • Border terrain type
  • Jail/camp structure
  • Village/street geography
  • Enemy hideout

For recurring objects, mention clearly:
  Map / File / Radio / Satellite image / Tunnel opening /
  Weapon / Passport / Clock / Old photograph

If a character changes their appearance (disguise, aging, injury),
note it explicitly when the change happens.

================================================================================
VOICE RULES
================================================================================

DEFAULT:
Strong declarative — narrator was there.

✅ "कमांडो ने 3 मिनट में hijacker neutralize कर दिया।"
✅ "24 मिसाइलें एक साथ नौ ठिकानों पर गिरीं।"
❌ "पुलिस के मुताबिक…" on every line.

Conversational hooks, sparingly:
  • "देखिए…"
  • "समझिए…"
  • "जरा सोचिए…"
  • "कल्पना कीजिए…"

Hindi: accessible, not Sanskritised.

English terms allowed where natural:
  Go ahead / target / green signal / operation / mission /
  neutralized / intelligence input / surveillance / briefing

Not a news bulletin. Not a classroom lecture.
Cinematic, urgent, visually alive.

