SUB-GENRE NOTES
================================================================================

COVERT / RAW / IB
  → Mole, surveillance, fake identity, border crossing, coded message,
     double agent, safe house, handler, months of patience.

CROSS-BORDER STRIKE
  → Target list, intel confirmation, political clearance,
     launch window, weapon path, enemy panic, official response.

MILITARY / AIR STRIKE
  → Aircraft type, runway, radar, missile path, weather, pilots,
     control room, target destruction, return to base.

ESCAPE / SURVIVAL
  → Jail/camp geography, guard routine, tunnel/route, hunger, cold,
     disguise, navigation, near-capture, final crossing.

MASTERMIND
  → Backroom strategy, old political experience, decision tree,
     reading people, silent moves, delayed payoff.

UNDERWORLD
  → Network, money route, police file, safe houses, fake names,
     betrayal, political/criminal protection, near arrest.

HISTORICAL
  → Era accuracy, colonial/political context, mystery, legacy,
     letters, meetings, train routes, uniforms, old maps.

POP-CULTURE TIE-IN
  → Start with known film/series character, reveal the real story.

